  "reviewer_note": "Contested figures, attributed: Ibrahim's army 100,000 and 1,000 elephants (what Babur was told) versus as low as 40,000; enemy dead 15,000-16,000 (Babur's men's estimate) versus 40,000-50,000 (Agra inhabitants), per historyofwar.org. The role of artillery is disputed: historyofwar.org says archers mattered most, the Smithsonian says neither guns nor elephants were critical. Babur's 12,000 is the count at the Indus crossing per historyofwar.org.",
